Package: decideR
Title: Bayesian Decision-Theoretic Actions under Loss and Hard Constraints
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Max",
           family = "Moldovan",
           email = "max.moldovan@adelaide.edu.au",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-9680-8474"))
Description: Maps a posterior distribution or an 'orchestra_manifest' inference result to an optimal action under an explicit loss function and a hard feasibility constraint, returning the action together with a grounding label and an honest abstention when evidence is insufficient. The grounding label is combined worst-case across inputs, so a decision resting on an unverified external fact is downgraded to abstention rather than asserted with false confidence. A manifest-native tail closes an analytics pipeline by deciding directly from an upstream member's inference result, and a grade-band loss prices quality-threshold ('protein-band') payoffs as a first-class step value schedule. Reference decisions cover bounded input-rate selection and constraint-capped position sizing.
